We are seeking a Paralegal, Privacy and Information Management to join our team. The Paralegal, Privacy and Information Management will support privacy programs, information governance, and regulatory compliance initiatives across the organization.

About the Role
In this role you will assist with privacy and information management activities, support policy implementation, conduct legal research, and coordinate cross-functional efforts to ensure compliance with applicable laws and regulatory requirements. You will work with legal, information security, and business teams to strengthen data governance, manage information lifecycle, and contribute to risk management efforts.

What you will do
- Support privacy program operations, information governance, and data lifecycle management
- Assist with regulatory requirements and compliance initiatives
- Conduct legal research related to privacy laws and regulatory developments
- Develop and maintain data glossary and standardized information definitions
- Support information security and data protection efforts, including risk assessment activities
- Assist with documentation for audits, incident response, and records management
- Coordinate workstreams and governance processes among the law department, security teams, and business stakeholders
- Stay current with federal and other applicable laws and regulatory requirements

Required Skills
- Data Privacy
- Information Security
- Information Management
- Regulatory Requirements
- Law Department Management
- Legal Research
- Data Glossary
- Security
- Federal Law
- Risk Management
- Information Gathering
- Workstream Governance
- Paralegals

What We Offer
- A collaborative and professional environment that values privacy, information governance, and responsible information management
- Opportunities for professional development and growth
- The chance to contribute to enterprise-wide privacy and information governance initiatives

How to Apply
Please submit your resume along with a brief cover letter outlining your interest and relevant experience related to privacy, information management, and regulatory compliance.

